Classify each request by its actual receiver. Before dismissing authentication:
- For Python, count the leading spaces on the with line and request line.
  A request aligned with with is outside the block; its mock has ended.
- Verify that the active replacement covers this client, method and destination.
  A separate live client or an explicit passthrough still reaches the service.
- A locally assigned fetch function or transport returning a fabricated Response
  intercepts its calls even when it never reads or checks the auth header.
- An ordinary readable account name in URL userinfo is not a secret, including
  in git clone/fetch. An opaque access token in that position is a credential.

